# Live development preview

The owner's VPS is the development environment. Every source change must be
synced there before the work is considered done. Do not wait to be asked.

- After editing, immediately copy the changed tracked source to the live
  development instance and rebuild or restart only the affected container.
  Consult ignored `AGENTS.local.md` for connection details. Never copy those
  details into tracked files, commits, or chat.
- Preserve volumes and runtime data. Never reset volumes or bring the stack
  down with volume wipes.
- Do not commit, push to Git, or open a pull request unless the owner
  explicitly asks.
- Never copy remote `.env`, compose overrides, databases, or other private
  runtime files into Git.
